{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1437072-the-sahara-probably-wasn-t-a-desert-in-the-age-of-irem","id":1437072,"title":"The Sahara probably wasn't a desert in the age of Irem.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-25T19:39:08-08:00","id":1437072,"title":"The Sahara probably wasn't a desert in the age of Irem.","content":"Assuming Irem was at its height around 3800 BC than most of the Sahara would have probably still been grassland. From the articles I have read it didn't become the desert it is today until around 2500 BC. <br /> <br /> I had been studying this when I discovered this cool map on Reddit.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://external-preview.redd.it/fhKhl1P_p5e05M2ZBxX5WSP2ezldAbS6uQa-LW0twnc.jpg?auto=webp&amp;s=cc0fc2066673fbddb9a14aea879d7cc510b75c0a\" target=\"_blank\">https://external-preview.redd.it/fhK...9d7cc510b75c0a</a><br /> <br /> Just something interesting I thought I would share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T19:58:53-08:00","id":1437074,"title":"","content":"Old Mummy acknowledged this and said part of the cause of desertification was the supernatural struggle with Sutekh.<br /> <br /> But I don't remember Irem contradicting this. It was a long ass time ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T12:21:10-08:00","id":1437133,"title":"","content":"I thought that the desertification of the Sahara was a direct result of the Rite of Return creating a wasteland. Either way that always confused me because much of Mummy history references the deserts beyond the Nile, which IS a historical error.<br /> <br /> I've tended to ignore that bit of fluff and had Irem a city in a near jungle at the Nile with Savannah's and large &quot;oases&quot; all around, and the mysterious deserts referenced being VERY far from it to the South and East. If a mummy ever remembered that far back that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T16:13:44-07:00","id":1443419,"title":"","content":"Do we have a firm enough date on the drying period to say that for sure one way or the other? Wikipedia unhelpfully places the time of the green sahara between 11,000 to 5,000 years ago. Osiris died in 5293 BC (he was killed on a Sothic Turn, and the next Turn is when the Rite of Return is invoked in 3832 BC, so working backwards...hurray math). The Shan'iatu spend a few centuries after murdering their god just sort of moping and hanging out beside the river, and we don't know when exactly they get the band back together and build the Nameless Empire. Mid-fourth millenia, presumably. From my understanding the Sahara desert probably does exist at this time, but the border between desert and savanna is much farther north than it is now (in other words, its much smaller). But that could still mean Irem is surrounded by deserts- references to the Sphinx in Dreams of Avarice imply it was built somewhere near ancient Heliopolis and modern Cairo. This could put it far enough North to be within reach of our baby Sahara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}